=====ADDITIONS for 1.3-1.4 (as of 6.21.26)=====
-Implant that stores a hyperseed of a miniturret or a specific prima weapon.
	-Seed lasts forever, but increases hunger rate
	-Fungal Tech

-Specialized psychic crystal that releases a scream of madness when shattered.
	-Madness can inflict a coma at high severities.
	-Can be created by corrupting an anima tree seed with meldtech.
	-Aquatic Tech

-Meldtech Dreamgate: A device that siphons mental energy from a pawn, putting them into a forced coma but otherwise leaving them unharmed.
	-The device appears as a small brazier, but doesn't need to be constantly connected to a pawn.
	-The resulting pearl can be used for any meldtech creations, and infinitely swapped around.
	-The pawn cannot be woken up in any way while in this coma state.
	-Unfortunately the process can be addictive.
	-Aquatic Tech

-Meldtech Spring: A coral spring that will replace specific terrains with similar ones with shallow waters.
	-These terrains allow meldtech plants and allow terratech plants.
	-They impose movement speed on those who haven't entered the bloodline, or don't have meldtech gear.
	-Aquatic Tech

-Stellar Core: A fragment of a star that acts as a portable sun. Both helpful and dangerous.
	-Initially releases 100% light, high temperature, and possible flares.
	-Allows creations that use solar energy to keep running, but can't override rest periods.
	-Will expire over time, generally over a few years.
		-Output also lowers, to a minimum of 50% light.
		-Generally what get's lowered is the radius and temperature.
	-Can be extracted from stellar creations.
	-Stellar Tech

-Meldtech Needle: a one-time item that knocks a pawn unconscious, into a Meldtech sleep.
	-Only lasts a few days.
	-Converts blood over time while the pawn is asleep.

-Ice buckler that a pawn wears and can activate.
	-Upon activation, forms an icy armor layer that is highly resistant to most damages.
	-Radiates extreme cold when being worn, affecting everyone within a medium radius.

-Frost scythe that inflicts wounds which are always frozen scars.
	-Builds up a 'soulfreeze' hefiff over time. When the pawn afflicted dies, a dropped item can be used to upgrade the weapon.
	-Each upgrade allows the scythe to consume and utilize more methods of psycast and anima energies.

-A staff formed of three different parts: a therma gem, an ebonwood staff, and a thunderblade.
	-When each three are seperated, they are quite powerful but also have ambient side effects.
	-When all three are combined, they form a powerful blade staff.
	-The staff allows the player to combine everything together.
		-It enables the player to use everything as a melee weapon.
		-The staff is the only part that needs to be renewed, so the weapon only requires brightsap.
	-The therma gem allows one to release temperatures of intense heat or cold that last a short while.
	-The blade allows the player to fire a bolt of powerful lightning, and deal EMP damage.
	-An AoE field can be created based on these effects.
	-This weapon is not upgraded, but the staff and blade can be used individually.
		-The therma gem is used in other temperature creations.


-A scythe formed in ice that condenses temperature over time.
	-The player can release the temperature as a mist.
		-The radius and temperature depends on how much they want to release.
	-An AoE field can be created that freezes an area, dealing high damage.

-Utilizing the book mechanic to add hints and guides into the game. These books can be sold to the player for
low prices.

